      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, in a corporate sense, \"boardroom presence\" is often deeply intertwined with established cultural norms of power presentation. Many ingrained executive cultures value a specific, reserved gravitas and highly polished, often indirect, communication style. Qualifications are necessary, but the *delivery*—how one occupies space and speaks—can trigger instant, subconscious judgments about leadership fitness. This can create a barrier where technical brilliance isn't automatically equated with commanding executive presence.",
